Better: replicate what `host()` does and let the exception escape:
```java
package io.github.diodeme.ji.cli;
public class VerifyHostLauncher {
  public static void main(String[] a) throws Exception {
    try (var app = LocalHostApplication.open(System.getenv())) { System.out.println(app.launchUri()); Thread.currentThread().join(); }
  }
}
```
`LocalHostApplication.open(Map)` is public. That will throw the real exception with stack trace. Compile into attachments dir (not repo) — it's a verification script, fine.

